# Call-site ledger of structlog at 8174a86a2f14b5bd295eded733ff5fffc12aa173.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in structlog.md.
#
# Supported versions: Python 3.10 and later (pyproject.toml: requires-python
# >=3.10). The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md.
# Role sets used below (structlog.md, "Role sets"):
#   Bound loggers (BL): BoundLoggerBase (public, plain class documented for
#     subclassing), structlog.BoundLogger (_generic), structlog.stdlib.BoundLogger,
#     structlog.twisted.BoundLogger, the six BoundLoggerFilteringAt* classes
#     that _make_filtering_bound_logger builds with type() (their methods are
#     the closures meth, ameth, log, alog, the functions _nop, _anop,
#     exception, aexception, and two lambdas), and structlog.stdlib.
#     AsyncBoundLogger (no BoundLoggerBase). No BoundLoggerBase subclass of
#     the package defines __init__, so instantiating one runs
#     BoundLoggerBase.__init__.
#   Wrapped loggers (W, the _logger of a bound logger and the first argument
#     of a processor): PrintLogger, WriteLogger, BytesLogger, ReturnLogger,
#     CapturingLogger, a logging.RootLogger for the empty factory name, or
#     a logging.Logger (stdlib.LoggerFactory; after it ran,
#     logging.getLogger makes _FixedFindCallerLogger objects), the module
#     twisted.python.log (twisted.LoggerFactory).
#   Logger factories (F): PrintLoggerFactory (default), WriteLoggerFactory,
#     BytesLoggerFactory, ReturnLoggerFactory, CapturingLoggerFactory,
#     stdlib.LoggerFactory, twisted.LoggerFactory, and the class PrintLogger
#     (tests/test_stdlib.py:1651).
#   Processors (P, 29): the functions merge_contextvars, add_log_level,
#     set_exc_info, filter_by_level, add_log_level_number, add_logger_name,
#     render_to_log_args_and_kwargs, render_to_log_kwargs, merge_threadlocal,
#     ProcessorFormatter.wrap_for_formatter and .remove_processors_meta, and
#     the __call__ of KeyValueRenderer, LogfmtRenderer, UnicodeEncoder,
#     UnicodeDecoder, JSONRenderer, ExceptionRenderer, TimeStamper,
#     MaybeTimeStamper, ExceptionPrettyPrinter, StackInfoRenderer,
#     CallsiteParameterAdder, EventRenamer, ConsoleRenderer,
#     PositionalArgumentsFormatter, ExtraAdder, LogCapture,
#     twisted.JSONRenderer, twisted.EventAdapter.
#   Contexts (C): dict (the default, and the type that Context =
#     dict[Any, Any] names, B4) and instances of wrap_dict classes
#     (_ThreadLocalDictWrapper subclasses, whose dict methods come from the
#     inner dict through __getattr__).
#   Optional imports run on both sides: rich, colorama, better_exceptions
#     and greenlet are not installed and are named as missing modules.
default reject structlog.__getattr__: the module __getattr__ of structlog runs only when an attribute of the module object structlog is missing; the only loads on that module are structlog.get_context (contextvars.py:77, threadlocal.py:252), which __init__.py:20 binds, and every `from structlog import ...` of a submodule runs before __init__.py:94 defines __getattr__
default reject structlog._config.BoundLoggerLazyProxy.__getattr__: no attribute load of the package misses the class and the instance dict of a BoundLoggerLazyProxy: its own methods read the seven attributes that __init__ (or __setstate__) sets, _context is a property, bind is a method or the instance attribute finalized_bind, and as_immutable and tmp_bind replace a proxy by logger.bind() first; a proxy is no wrapped logger, processor, context or event-dict value (B3)
default reject structlog._generic.BoundLogger.__getattr__: no attribute load of the package misses the class and the instance dict of a generic BoundLogger: BoundLoggerBase and as_immutable read _logger, _processors and _context, which __init__ (or __setstate__) sets, and methods of the class; the generic BoundLogger is never the wrapped logger (the entries accept it where a client attribute name is looked up on a bound logger)
default reject structlog._greenlets.GreenThreadLocal.__getattr__, structlog._greenlets.GreenThreadLocal.__setattr__: a GreenThreadLocal exists only as the _tl class attribute that wrap_dict puts on a WrappedDict class (threadlocal.py:96, when greenlet is importable); the only attributes loaded or stored on it are dict_ (threadlocal.py:123, 194, 196, 198, accepted there), and its own methods use __dict__ and _weakdict, which its instance dict holds
default reject structlog.testing.CapturingLogger.__getattr__: CapturingLogger reaches the wrapped-logger role, including stdlib.BoundLogger through the explicit constructor inputs in tests/test_stdlib.py:59-63,389 and tests/conftest.py:69-71. Entries accept its missing-attribute lookup in bound-logger dispatch and the stdlib passthrough bodies; its own calls attribute is initialized. Separate stdlib processor logger parameters are annotated logging.Logger and have no named CapturingLogger input evidence, so those roles and unrelated receivers do not admit it.
default reject structlog.threadlocal._ThreadLocalDictWrapper.__getattr__: a _ThreadLocalDictWrapper is only the context of a bound logger whose context_class is a wrap_dict class, or an instance of that class; the entries accept this candidate at dict-method forwarding (copy, pop, clear, update, keys) and when a lazy _dict getter raises AttributeError during the same lookup on an admitted dict subclass constructor; every other receiver is a str, bytes, dict, list, tuple, module, class, stream, frame, record, event dict or another object that is no wrapper
default reject structlog._base.BoundLoggerBase.__eq__, structlog.threadlocal._ThreadLocalDictWrapper.__eq__, structlog.twisted.ReprWrapper.__eq__: no operand of this comparison, `in` test or dict lookup is a bound logger, a wrapped context or a ReprWrapper: the operands are str, bytes, ints, None, tuples of streams, classes, enum members, sys.exc_info() tuples and dict keys of those types; the entries accept the candidates where a context is compared (_base.py:67) or __eq__ is called explicitly
default reject structlog.threadlocal._ThreadLocalDictWrapper.__len__, structlog.threadlocal._ThreadLocalDictWrapper.__iter__, structlog.threadlocal._ThreadLocalDictWrapper.__setitem__: no wrapped context is truth-tested, measured, iterated, searched with `in` or assigned into by subscript in the package: event dicts are copies made by .copy() (a plain dict, also for a wrapped context, whose copy is that of its inner dict) or dicts built by ProcessorFormatter, and every other operand is a str, bytes, tuple, list, dict, set, frame, class, stream or the wrapped logger (none of which is a wrapper)
default reject structlog._base.BoundLoggerBase.__repr__, structlog._config.BoundLoggerLazyProxy.__repr__, structlog._output.BytesLogger.__repr__, structlog._output.PrintLogger.__repr__, structlog._output.WriteLogger.__repr__, structlog.testing.CapturingLogger.__repr__, structlog.threadlocal._ThreadLocalDictWrapper.__repr__, structlog.twisted.ReprWrapper.__repr__: the formatted, printed, str()'d or repr()'d value is a str, bytes, number, class, module, stream, UUID, exception, tuple of client arguments, a client value of an event dict or a processor (no processor class defines __repr__ or __str__); the entries accept the candidates where a context, a wrapped logger or a frame local is formatted

